seem to contradict one another.

29
00:01:29,241 --> 00:01:33,454
In this portion especially, Rashi shows deep concern

30
00:01:33,494 --> 00:01:36,494
for the ethical dimensions of the law, reading

31
00:01:36,561 --> 00:01:40,734
moral psychology into individual word choices and grammatical

32
00:01:40,827 --> 00:01:45,236
forms.Let's begin with the very first verse of

33
00:01:45,276 --> 00:01:48,836
our portion: "You shall truly tithe all the

34
00:01:48,898 --> 00:01:52,756
increase of your seed." Rashi immediately asks a

35
00:01:52,814 --> 00:01:54,036
structural question.

36
00:01:54,256 --> 00:01:56,685
Why does the Torah place the tithing laws

37
00:01:56,845 --> 00:01:59,965
here, right after the preceding passage?

38
00:02:00,165 --> 00:02:02,125
His answer is striking.

39
00:02:02,365 --> 00:02:06,205
God is essentially saying to Israel: do not

40
00:02:06,272 --> 00:02:08,605
